### Completed source stages

1. Campaign Task 1: deterministic discovery/confirmation/qualification panel ownership, sealed
   commitments, one-use stage ledgers, attempt/outcome contracts, and content-free verification.
2. Campaign Task 2: canonical authenticated manifests, graph-before-parse verification, clean source
   capture, and non-executable readiness rendering.
3. Campaign Task 3: two complete provider-free feedback rounds through the normal V5 runtime, three
   behavior variants per round, full critic direction restored to the next investigator, zero
   external usage, source unchanged, cleanup complete. This proves orchestration and variant
   mechanics only, not production performance.
4. Campaign Task 6: source-only one-use confirmation adapter. It freezes one reducer-authenticated
   final discovery champion, opens the ledger before held-out deserialization, retires every terminal
   path, and has confirmation-owned crash recovery.
5. Campaign Task 7: source-only detached qualification adapter. It recomputes confirmation
   eligibility, binds the immutable target and shared evidence identities, gates success on active,
   causal-clean net annualized return that reaches target and strictly beats the same-panel baseline,
   and supports cleanup-only recovery without re-evaluation.
6. Campaign Task 8: source-only full-replay readiness. It emits create-only, content-free,
   non-executable projections only from a successful retired qualification graph. Its source
   inspection pins trusted Windows Git and all tracked source through output creation, disables
   executable Git behavior, rejects unsafe checkout forms, and has no replay launch path.

